"kind": "rich",
"html": "\n<section class=\"section service-editorial\"><div class=\"shell service-reading\"><nav class=\"service-jump-links\" aria-label=\"On this service page\"><a href=\"#service-work\">Services</a><a href=\"#service-method\">Repair &amp; installation</a><a href=\"#service-quote\">Costs &amp; quote</a><a href=\"#service-faq\">FAQs</a><a href=\"#service-booking\">Book a visit</a></nav><aside class=\"service-answer\" data-service-answer><h2>What to do next</h2><p>Describe whether the tap drips, water appears around its base, or a connection leaks below the fixture. You do not need to dismantle the fitting. Keep clear of water near electrical equipment and report concealed connections from a safe position. We assess fitting condition, compatible parts and access before recommending repair or replacement. For a new mixer, the written quote distinguishes the product from installation and any connection work.</p><p><a href=\"insights-reporting-a-plumbing-leak.html\">Describe the location and timing of a leak</a>. <a href=\"contact.html?service=tap-mixer-repairs-perth.html\">Request an assessment and written quote</a>.</p></aside><div id=\"service-work\" class=\"service-editorial-part\"><h2>Kitchen, bathroom and laundry tap repairs</h2><h3>Dripping taps and leaking mixer fittings</h3><p>A persistent drip and water appearing around the base or under a cabinet are different symptoms. We inspect the relevant fitting and accessible connections to define the repair. Tell us where the water appears and whether it occurs while the tap is running or when it is off; there is no need to dismantle the tap first.</p>\n<h3>Stiff controls, uneven delivery and fixture faults</h3><p>Controls that become difficult to move, inconsistent flow and a fitting that no longer operates properly can involve different components or connection conditions. Our plumber assesses the fitting type and condition before selecting a repair. A symptom at one tap is not automatically evidence that the whole property needs new pipework.</p>\n<h3>Replacing a tap or mixer during an upgrade</h3><p>If you want a replacement rather than a repair, we assess the mounting arrangement, accessible connections and compatibility of the proposed fitting. Send the product details if you already have a selection. For broader fixture and appliance connections, see our <a href=\"fixtures-appliances-perth.html\">fixture and appliance installation services</a>.</p><figure class=\"service-editorial-figure\"><img loading=\"lazy\"\n            class=\"service-editorial-image\"\n            src=\"plumbing-leak-perth.png\"\n            width=\"1672\"\n            height=\"941\"\n            alt=\"Kitchen plumbing connection being inspected\"\n             srcset=\"plumbing-leak-perth-480.webp 480w, plumbing-leak-perth-800.webp 800w, plumbing-leak-perth-1200.webp 1200w\" sizes=\"(max-width:700px) 100vw, (max-width:1000px) 50vw, 380px\"></figure></div>\n<div id=\"service-method\" class=\"service-editorial-part\"><h2>How we plan tap repairs and mixer replacement</h2><p>We establish the fitting type, reported problem and available access above and below the fixture. Compatible parts and the condition of the existing fitting influence whether a repair is practical. We explain that assessment rather than assuming that either a small part or a complete replacement is always the right choice.</p>\n<h3>Match the fitting to the existing installation</h3><p>Replacement needs to suit the fixture and connection arrangement, not just the appearance of the tap. Concealed connections or restricted cabinet access can change the work required. The quote identifies the fitting, connection work and any additional access so you know whether product supply and installation are both included.</p>\n<p>After the authorised work, we check the repaired or replaced fitting and the relevant connections. We explain the completed scope and any separate issue observed around the installation. If the water source is unclear or extends beyond the fitting, our <a href=\"water-leak-detection-perth.html\">plumbing leak detection service</a> addresses that investigation without treating it as a routine tap replacement.</p></div><p class=\"service-trade-note\">Our Perth plumbing and electrical work is carried out by appropriately licensed trades. Licence details are available on request.</p><p class=\"service-safety\"><strong>Safety:</strong> Do not dismantle concealed plumbing or approach water near electrical equipment to investigate. Describe the problem from a safe position. For immediate danger, Call 000.</p><!-- keyword-gap:start --><div class=\"keyword-gap-content\" data-keyword-gap><div class=\"keyword-gap-part\" id=\"learn-about-tap-mixer-repairs-perth\"><h2>Tap repairs Perth: symptoms and service choices</h2><h3>Tap drips after shut-off</h3><p>A sealing component or another fitting fault may allow water through. A mixer leaking at its base is a different observation from a drip at the outlet. The fitting and parts need assessment before choosing repair or replacement.</p><h3>Water lost through a persistent drip</h3><p>Yes. A persistent drip can add up, with the amount depending on its flow and duration. We do not estimate a saving from the sound alone; arrange assessment and compare the agreed repair or replacement option.</p><h3>Installing a customer-supplied replacement mixer</h3><p>Yes, subject to suitability. Discuss the model and existing connection before purchase so the quote can identify installation, any additional parts and whether other access work is needed.</p><ul class=\"intent-links\"><li><a href=\"fixtures-appliances-perth.html\">Fitting compatibility and connection scope</a></li></ul></div></div><!-- keyword-gap:end --></div></section>" as TrustedHtml
},
